MoBetta: x87sidecar: Bridge x87 runs across push/pop and mov [m],imm.

Run bridging joins x87 runs across short gaps of mov/lea/flag-dead ALU, but
not across stack pushes and pops or stores of an immediate. WoW 3.3.5a's
segment-vs-box test (0x7f9480, 5.8% of the game thread at the Dalaran
fountain) has `mov; push ebx; push esi; mov`, `push edi; lea; lea` and
`movl $1,-0x4(%ebp)` between its x87 ops, so each op went one per reply,
converting its 80-bit slot in and out. In the Dalaran capture, push was the
biggest blocker of all (5.2% of Wow.exe time at run boundaries).

New bridge shapes, all flag-free (no liveness proof needed):
- push r / pop r of a 32/64-bit GPR other than ESP/RSP. Rosetta decodes them
  as push/pop with a 64-bit operand in 64-bit code and pushd/popd with a
  32-bit operand in 32-bit code; the pairing gives the stack width. Lowered
  to SUB+STR / LDR+ADD on x4; the 32-bit forms use W arithmetic (ESP wraps
  at 32 bits) and the 32-bit pop addresses through a W-copy of ESP, since a
  32-bit guest register's upper half is not guaranteed zero. push/pop esp,
  16-bit forms and push imm (no operand size) stay with stock.
- mov m32/m64, imm (BridgeStoreGI). The node keeps mem_operand; the
  immediate is read from the next operand of the same IRInstr at lowering.
All three are barriers for load sinking and fence off pass_fma_reduce, like
the other bridge stores and register writes.

Default X87_BRIDGE_MAX_GAP 2 -> 4 and X87_BRIDGE_MAX_TOTAL 8 -> 16 (both
already in range): WoW's gaps run 3-4 instructions, and at 2 / 8 the new
shapes join almost nothing there (offline, Dalaran: +2.9% of Wow.exe time
at joinable boundaries at gap 2, +9.0% at gap 4, +10.3% at 16).

A memory fault inside a joined region behaves as for any store inside a
run today (aborts without X87_PRECISE_FAULTS); Wine commits thread stacks
up front, so a push only faults on a real stack overflow.

Tests: tests/test_bridge_stack.c (push/pop around x87 ops that address
through the moved RSP, x87 store read back by pop, two pushes and pops,
pop as the next base, mov [m],imm 32/64/zero/high-bit); suite 1450 passed,
0 failed, 2 known stock divergences, at both the old and the new defaults.
MoBetta tests/x87_bridge_stack.c (0x7f9480 instruction for instruction,
32-bit push/pop/imm mix): bit-identical to stock Rosetta, loop ~595 -> ~530
ms. Session #28 Dalaran profile: 22.86 -> 21.55 ARM per x87 op. In game at
the Dalaran fountain: 45-50 FPS vs 40-50 on the previous sidecar.

